<title>USA: StreamLogic says faces June 27 delisting.</title>
<headline>StreamLogic says faces June 27 delisting.</headline>
<dateline>MENLO PARK, Calif. 1997-06-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>StreamLogic Corp said Tuesday it faces delisting from the Nasdaq Stock Market June 27 because it no longer meets its requirements.</p>
<p>The company said its stock price, market capitalization and net tangible assets are to low for Nasdaq inclusion.</p>
<p>StreamLogic said it was notified by Nasdaq that the company may no longer meet the criteria for continued inclusion in its stock market.</p>
<p>StreamLogic closed Monday at 1/8.</p>
